rediction grants with an own fresh member, including null. PLAN.md identifies this concrete body-output seam for source review; it needs honest union narrowing, no Grant cast.\n\nWhen that no-fresh value wins existing first-qualified selection, any declared observes row returns the existing authority-unavailable result before settlement. Earlier field/subject/row-size checks keep their order. No separate supplied proof or empty subject list can rescue those rows. This requires an explicit body-only boundary: settle can otherwise serve separate observations. Ordinary Grant/prediction and mark paths that never select this value stay unchanged; generic observes code stays unchanged.\n\n**Evidence plan.** Strengthen the existing forms-grant “one table” order case with wrong-key+revoked+old and old+missing-action; run the same whole owner before/after. Extend existing body/observes cases, not a per-field suite. One observes-stop control must distinguish with a separately supplied valid fresh fixture read; exact mutation waits for reviewed code. Compile-only assignments reject the value as Grant, Presented, runtime authority and replay context; unchanged isGrant also rejects the missing own fresh field. Runtime may independently acquire genuine authority, so rejection of this supplied value is not a promise that the whole act refuses.\n\nKeep oracle owners, fixture bytes/digests/answers and definition corpus unchanged. Later run only maintained compare mode, with capture unset, and report actual completed owners/counts; no new capture/adoption. No oracle owner gains calls. Document this second E1-form exception in kernel section 7 with the owner's date and the runtime/replay corpus condition.\n\nProposed production scope: grant.ts, judge.ts and the kernel paragraph, plus bounded existing-owner/type witnesses. No Client, standing-source, MCP, contract wire, runtime/replay implementation, E2 or E3 change. Raw file copies/hashes and the full boundary/type rationale are in raw-source-bindings.json and PLAN.md. All checks remain UNRUN.\n","to":"planner"}}